---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';

// Written against what the code actually does, not from a template. Every
// claim below was checked: the third-party origins in the built output, the
// absence of any analytics, the self-hosted fonts, the one localStorage key,
// and what worker/index.ts sends to Buttondown and logs locally.
//
// If the signup path changes, this page changes with it.
const updated = '15 October 2026';
const contact = 'privacy@rodeooh.rodeo';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What the Rodeo waitlist collects, who processes it, and how to get it deleted."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-6 py-16">
      <Eyebrow>Privacy</Eyebrow>
      <h1 class="display m-0 max-w-[16ch] text-[clamp(38px,6.5vw,60px)]">What we keep</h1>

      <div
        class="max-w-[680px] border-l-2 border-yellow bg-field-raised py-4 pl-4 pr-5 font-mono text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-legend"
      >
        The short version: the waitlist stores your email address at Buttondown
        so we can email you about Rodeo. There is no analytics, no advertising,
        no tracking, and nothing is sold or shared. Unsubscribe from any email,
        or write to {contact} and it is deleted.
      </div>

      <div class="post max-w-[680px] pt-2">
        <h2>What the waitlist collects</h2>
        <p>
          Three things, when you submit the form and only then:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Your email address.</strong> Stored at Buttondown. It is
            the whole point of the form.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your IP address</strong>, passed to Buttondown with the
            signup as a spam signal. It is not stored by us.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Which page you signed up from</strong> — a short label like
            <code>home</code> or <code>log-post</code>. This is written to our
            own server log and sent nowhere. Your address is never written to
            that log.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The legal basis is your consent. Nothing is sent until you click the
          link in the confirmation email, and Buttondown records the date and
          time you did, which is what makes the consent demonstrable.
        </p>

        <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
        <h3>Buttondown — United States</h3>
        <p>
          The email list itself. Buttondown holds your address and the record
          of your consent, sends the confirmation email and the newsletter, and
          handles unsubscribes. They act as a processor on our instructions,
          under a data processing agreement that uses Standard Contractual
          Clauses for transfers out of the UK and EU. Their policy:
          <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy">buttondown.com/legal/privacy</a>.
        </p>
        <h3>Cloudflare — United States</h3>
        <p>
          Hosts this site and runs the small piece of code that handles the
          signup. Cloudflare sees what any web host sees — your IP address,
          your browser's user agent, and which page you asked for — and retains
          it briefly as operational logs. Cloudflare also provides Turnstile,
          the "verify you are human" check on the signup form, which exists to
          stop bots filling the list. Their policy:
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a>,
          and the processing terms:
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/">their customer DPA</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is the complete list. No one else receives anything.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>No analytics.</strong> No page-view counter, no heatmaps,
            no session recording, no advertising or conversion pixels of any
            kind.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No cookies of our own.</strong> We set none. Cloudflare may
            set one as part of the Turnstile check on the signup form.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No fonts loaded from anyone else.</strong> All 28 font
            files are served from this domain. Loading Google Fonts from
            Google's own servers has been found to breach the GDPR in German
            case law, and avoiding it costs nothing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>One third-party script, on one form.</strong> Turnstile, on
            the signup form only. Nothing else on the site loads code from
            another origin.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Stored in your browser</h2>
        <p>
          The <a href="/sdk/">rodeo-sdk documentation</a> saves a display
          preference under the key <code>starlight-theme</code>. It stays on
          your device, is never transmitted, and clearing your browser data
          removes it. Nothing else on the site stores anything locally.
        </p>

        <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Your email address:</strong> until you unsubscribe or ask
            for it to be deleted. There is no other expiry — if the Kickstarter
            is years away, the list waits.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>An address that never confirms:</strong> stays unactivated
            and is never emailed again.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Server logs:</strong> held by Cloudflare for a short
            operational window and not copied anywhere else.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask for a copy of what is held about you, have it corrected,
          have it deleted, have it sent to you in a portable form, or withdraw
          your consent — and withdrawing it is as easy as giving it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <strong>unsubscribe link in every email</strong> is the fastest
          route and needs no reply from anyone. For anything else, write to
          <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. Deletion is permanent and
          we do not keep a suppression copy unless you ask us to.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this page changes in a way that affects what is collected or who
          sees it, the change is announced in the build log rather than quietly
          slipped in. Last updated {updated}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
